Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Matter contributions to the graviton self-energy", "Title",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"ea18b485-5df7-449e-bfba-4f4444571a35"],

Cell["\<\
Explore Dirac-fermion, massive-vector, massless-vector and SU(N) gluon, ghost \
and quark contributions to the graviton self-energy. Each sector combines \
contact and bubble diagrams, checks the full tadpole-dependent Ward \
identities and a polarisation-projected contraction, and decomposes the \
resulting tensor. The scalar-loop section is not included in this version.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"a0913169-f191-495c-a02a-a20241999d3f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Setup and notation", "Section",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"36e4b7e4-c248-4ad6-bd93-3b8eac7e68e0"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh Mathematica kernel and evaluate the input cells from top \
to bottom (Shift+Enter). Install FeynGrav and its FeynCalc dependency first; \
see the package README. Opening this notebook executes nothing. A semicolon \
stores an intermediate result without printing its full expression. Use \
?FunctionName for help and FeynGravCommands[] to discover the package \
interface.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"343a6c8b-f813-467f-8277-ead69bf1c5c8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"<<", "\"\<FeynGrav`\>\""}], ";"}]], "Input",
 Editable->False,
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{4.00009664861095*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"efb5c4a7-7a16-4360-8fe4-80d12cda7a98"],

Cell["\<\
This notebook uses the development-branch FeynGravSimplify interface and \
requires FORM on the kernel's PATH. LoopMomenta -> {k} requests integral \
reduction in FORM; PaVeToABCD displays the resulting scalar master integrals. \
Evaluate in a fresh kernel with symbolic D.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"a2fc4fc2-bd9d-46fd-a918-254cbdb6ed2b"],

Cell["\<\
Explicit expands propagator shorthand before export. The fermion contact \
trace is evaluated by FORM; the other displayed Dirac traces are evaluated \
with DiracSimplify before export. SUNSimplify contracts colour indices, with \
SUNNToCACF -> False retaining SUNN. Collect and Factor organise the reduced \
expressions; they do not supply diagram weights.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"85a7c34b-9a5b-4e00-bbae-7307cc38f0a5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The external momentum is p, the integration momentum is k and m is the \
matter mass where present. Repeated indices are summed. LoopMomenta -> {k} \
preserves integral interpretation even when denominator cancellations leave a \
polynomial; DropScaleless -> True removes scaleless integrals, but retains \
massive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8aea0ac2-f10f-4e8b-84b8-193fa9e021a6"],
 " tadpoles. The reduction uses the FeynCalc ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"\[ImaginaryI]", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Pi]", "2"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"9cd38095-05fc-42e1-a9f3-00e80f66d0b9"],
 " normalisation without an extra ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "2", " ", "\[Pi]", ")"}], 
    RowBox[{"-", "D"}]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "6511511c-d932-48d2-813a-325d6a017843"],
 " measure. No ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"D", "\[Rule]", "4"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"c88d2074-c744-4129-9f5d-b7878b3b8638"],
 " substitution or UV subtraction is made."
}], "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"fd20420e-ebd5-4b06-b425-8bb3fca8108a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "FeynGrav supplies the vertex and propagator factors of i and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Kappa]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8254b15d-207b-4e3d-8760-48be6bad2a4a"],
 ". The notebook supplies the additional diagram weights: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   FractionBox["1", "2"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "865c56fc-5ad3-406f-ac75-bec9b9300745"],
 " for real-boson contact and bubble loops, and -1 for closed Dirac or \
complex ghost loops. Use the package's fresh-kernel gauge defaults. The \
gravitational GaugeFixingEpsilon default is 2; this is distinct from the \
vector and Yang-Mills gauge settings."
}], "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"cf167e0d-22aa-4c9b-8652-0ffba68fac81"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FeynGravImportSUNYM", "[", "2", "]"}], ";"}]], "Input",
 Editable->False,
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"7dd18be5-e2f1-4515-bdfc-16cc8969eead"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["3. Dirac fermion loop", "Section",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"c99f528a-187e-4dd4-8dac-ff3e634e0502"],

Cell["\<\
A single massive Dirac field contributes a two-graviton contact loop and a \
bubble. Both definitions include the closed-fermion-loop minus sign. The \
propagator numerators use the routing required by the displayed vertex \
arguments. The contact trace is passed to FORM; the bubble trace is evaluated \
with DiracSimplify before export.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"021b0f51-e7ae-492a-8134-3b205eb2776a"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Tadpole contributions", "Subsection",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"d193e724-b597-44f8-9499-a623c11bfd93"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Close the two matter legs of a vertex with two external gravitons. This \
two-point contact diagram is often called a tadpole diagram; it is distinct \
from the one-external-graviton amplitude that appears in the full Ward \
identity. Its massive ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", "0"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "9872f5e5-1ce4-4581-9cb4-3ba92a41cfb5"],
 " contribution must be retained."
}], "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"c905082d-07d2-46ff-96b4-2e3d8451e249"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion1", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"PaVeToABCD", "[", 
    RowBox[{"FeynGravSimplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
       RowBox[{"-", 
        RowBox[{"DiracTrace", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{
             "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "p", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]",
               ",", 
              RowBox[{"-", "p"}]}], "}"}], ",", "k", ",", 
            RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], ".", 
          RowBox[{"QuarkPropagator", "[", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"LoopMomenta", "->", 
       RowBox[{"{", "k", "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"DropScaleless", "->", "True"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 Editable->False,
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000096899381507*^9, 4.000096899626433*^9}, {
  4.000097454156126*^9, 4.0000975084922*^9}, {4.000097661787676*^9, 
  4.000097665384454*^9}, {4.0016535599460297`*^9, 4.0016536163698606`*^9}, {
  4.0017237074185534`*^9, 4.001723710656036*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[3]:=",ExpressionUUID->"f9d98ece-554e-49e6-9832-16c1fd32ef07"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Bubble contributions", "Subsection",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"25975c49-5b57-4bd3-a721-e8c9ff0a7476"],

Cell["\<\
Join the two matter\[Dash]graviton vertices with the indicated propagators. \
The integrand specifies the momentum routing; k is the integration variable.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"c6c58ee4-3cae-4213-b2db-826757650c03"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion2", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"PaVeToABCD", "[", 
    RowBox[{"FeynGravSimplify", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"DiracSimplify", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Explicit", "[", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"DiracTrace", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "p"}], "}"}], ",", "k", ",", 
              RowBox[{"-", 
               RowBox[{"(", 
                RowBox[{"p", "+", "k"}], ")"}]}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], ".", 
            RowBox[{"QuarkPropagator", "[", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "}"}], "]"}], ".", 
            RowBox[{"GravitonFermionVertex", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", 
                RowBox[{"-", "p"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"p", "+", "k"}], ",", 
              RowBox[{"-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "]"}], ".", 
            RowBox[{"QuarkPropagator", "[", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"-", "p"}], "-", "k"}], ",", "m"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], 
           "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"DiracTraceEvaluate", "->", "True"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"LoopMomenta", "->", 
       RowBox[{"{", "k", "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"DropScaleless", "->", "True"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 Editable->False,
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000097517226603*^9, 4.000097558271748*^9}, {
   4.000097628472246*^9, 4.000097639678172*^9}, 4.0000976699001493`*^9, {
   4.001723716853264*^9, 4.0017237507442303`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"aafaf6c7-3a6e-408c-a227-6c5ebf993c2d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Combined tensor", "Subsection",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"d830ff05-6f20-470a-8bd0-58d7da9db280"],

Cell["\<\
Add the contact and bubble amplitudes. Their definitions include the \
real-boson symmetry factor 1/2 or the closed-Dirac/ghost-loop sign -1, as \
appropriate. Colour multiplicities are retained.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"ea7b7aea-ab78-4f57-9d6e-bbbc0752c367"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion", "[", 
    RowBox[{
    "\[Mu]_", ",", "\[Nu]_", ",", "\[Alpha]_", ",", "\[Beta]_", ",", "p_", ",",
      "m_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion1", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
        "m"}], "]"}], "+", 
      RowBox[{"GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion2", "[", 
       RowBox[{
       "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", 
        "m"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"A0", "[", "__", "]"}], ",", 
       RowBox[{"B0", "[", "__", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Collect", "[", 
       RowBox[{"#1", ",", "m", ",", "Factor"}], "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 Editable->False,
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[5]:=",ExpressionUUID->"a05e6ff7-20c3-4882-85d6-947379b6875a"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Full tadpole-dependent Ward identities", "Subsection",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"e5d8841b-3b8c-42fe-95ad-d165f4eabf39"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The one-external-graviton loop has the form ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["T", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}]], "=", "t", " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[Eta]", 
     RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"cdd5e7e3-ec6a-4fe5-8ee2-5a223b422f2f"],
 ". The first cell computes t by contracting its two indices and dividing by \
D. This one-point function is different from the two-graviton contact loop \
calculated above. Both use the same loop normalisation and diagram weights. \
The massive one-point function is retained; no vacuum-energy subtraction is \
made."
}], "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"b826512e-79f9-4224-a792-a596f60f13d5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"gravitonTadpoleFermion", "=", "PaVeToABCD", "[", "FeynGravSimplify",
   "[", "Contract", "[", "MTD", "[", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", "]", " ", "(",
   "-", "DiracSimplify", "[", "Explicit", "[", "DiracTrace", "[", 
  "GravitonFermionVertex", "[", "{", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "0", "}",
   ",", "k", ",", "-", "k", ",", "m", "]", ".", "QuarkPropagator", "[", "{", "-",
   "k", ",", "m", "}", "]", "]", "]", ",", "DiracTraceEvaluate", "->", "True",
   "]", ")", "]", "/", "D", ",", "LoopMomenta", "->", "{", "k", "}", ",", 
  "DropScaleless", "->", "True", "]", "]", ";"}]], "Input",
 Editable->False,
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[6]:=",ExpressionUUID->"1b47420a-f0a1-4881-9f80-0023742ae2f2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The four checks contract the self-energy with p on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Mu]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "8229b386-58e3-4abe-bc45-ad6e63d74c79"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Nu]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "cc98d136-f504-4d4f-9d69-3e94e4705761"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Alpha]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "21a0eb54-5de0-4f53-89c8-65a380437fe1"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox["\[Beta]", TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "faae794e-689a-4c45-8ac9-2e76512c80fa"],
 ", respectively, and add the corresponding one-point contribution. For the \
first contraction the residual is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["p", "\[Mu]"], " ", 
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPi]", 
     RowBox[{"\[Mu]", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}]], "+", 
    FractionBox[
     RowBox[{"\[Kappa]", " ", "t"}], "2"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     SuperscriptBox["p", "\[Alpha]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Eta]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "\[Beta]"}]], "+", 
     SuperscriptBox["p", "\[Beta]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Eta]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Nu]", "\[Alpha]"}]], "-", 
     SuperscriptBox["p", "\[Nu]"], " ", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Eta]", 
      RowBox[{"\[Alpha]", "\[Beta]"}]], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"42deadb8-4ee9-43f1-9351-41822bca1300"],
 ". Each check leaves three indices free, keeps D symbolic and uses no \
polarisation constraints or on-shell substitution. Each result should be \
True. These checks test the full two-point Ward identity; they do not by \
themselves fix every transverse coefficient or perform renormalisation."
}], "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"fe016dcf-b054-4827-b620-d1f02808517d"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Factor", "[", "FeynGravSimplify", "[", "FVD", "[", "p", ",", 
  "\[Mu]", "]", " ", "GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion", "[", "\[Mu]", ",",
   "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", "m", "]", "+", 
  "\[Kappa]", " ", "gravitonTadpoleFermion", "/", "2", " ", "(", "FVD", "[", 
  "p", ",", "\[Alpha]", "]", " ", "MTD", "[", "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Beta]", "]", "+",
   "FVD", "[", "p", ",", "\[Beta]", "]", " ", "MTD", "[", "\[Nu]", ",", 
  "\[Alpha]", "]", "-", "FVD", "[", "p", ",", "\[Nu]", "]", " ", "MTD", "[", 
  "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", "]", ")", "]", "]", "==", "0"}]], "Input",
 Editable->False,
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b4e9b2ff-39e0-4d12-8ced-623bb77878ee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox["True", TraditionalForm]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.0017260388268433`*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[7]=",ExpressionUUID->"54b34b7f-591e-453f-ade5-3d83215df0d7"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Factor", "[", "FeynGravSimplify", "[", "FVD", "[", "p", ",", 
  "\[Nu]", "]", " ", "GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion", "[", "\[Mu]", ",",
   "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", "m", "]", "+", 
  "\[Kappa]", " ", "gravitonTadpoleFermion", "/", "2", " ", "(", "FVD", "[", 
  "p", ",", "\[Alpha]", "]", " ", "MTD", "[", "\[Mu]", ",", "\[Beta]", "]", "+",
   "FVD", "[", "p", ",", "\[Beta]", "]", " ", "MTD", "[", "\[Mu]", ",", 
  "\[Alpha]", "]", "-", "FVD", "[", "p", ",", "\[Mu]", "]", " ", "MTD", "[", 
  "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", "]", ")", "]", "]", "==", "0"}]], "Input",
 Editable->False,
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"746baab2-2d1e-452b-a98d-b696f4a3664d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox["True", TraditionalForm]], "Output",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001726038985096*^9},
 CellLabel->"Out[8]=",ExpressionUUID->"1cfdda3e-090a-44c0-9f4e-4caaa461dfb5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Factor", "[", "FeynGravSimplify", "[", "FVD", "[", "p", ",", 
  "\[Alpha]", "]", " ", "GravitonPolarizationOperatorFermion", "[", "\[Mu]", ",",
   "\[Nu]", ",", "\[Alpha]", ",", "\[Beta]", ",", "p", ",", "m", "]", "+", 
  "\[Kappa]", " ", "gravitonTadpoleFermion", "/", "2", " ", "(", "FVD", "[", 
