Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["How to adapt this example", "Section",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"33d49ce3-0c25-45aa-a859-c3a5c575a38b"],

Cell["\<\
Change one mass, routing or field content at a time and recompute all \
dependent definitions and tables in a fresh kernel. Change every affected \
vertex and propagator consistently when rerouting a loop. These are \
unrenormalised self-energies: no vacuum-energy subtraction, UV subtraction or \
Laurent expansion has been performed. A projected zero or a tensor \
decomposition alone does not validate every coefficient. Treat saved outputs \
as results of their recorded evaluations, not a substitute for rerunning \
changed inputs.\
\>", "Text",
 Editable->False,ExpressionUUID->"a6dab477-b229-411c-bd85-6aef82cd945a"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]]
},
